title: >-
  Ungrounded: Entity Grounding Failure Drives Spurious
  Internal-Tool Invocation in LLM Agents
message: If you use this software or data, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Taran
    family-names: SURNAME
    affiliation: Shroud Labs Limited
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/USERNAME/ungrounded'
abstract: >-
  Harnesses, raw per-trial data and analysis for four studies
  (13,470 trials, six models, two vendors) measuring spurious
  decoy-tool invocation by benign LLM agents, and identifying
  entity grounding failure as the driving mechanism.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - Model Context Protocol
  - deception technology
  - canary tokens
  - tool selection
  - agent security
